<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <style name="Theme.MyApplication" parent="android:Theme.DeviceDefault.NoActionBar" />

    <!--
      Phase 51.1 — the cold start is CodeC, not black.

      Before this, the launcher activity used Theme.MyApplication directly and
      the first frame a user met on every cold start was the system window
      background (a black or white rectangle) while MainActivity.onCreate built
      the world. This style paints that first frame with the app's own mark on
      the app's own surface:

        * windowSplashScreenBackground = @color/codec_splash_background
          (#101418 — the same value the launcher art already uses, pinned by
          SplashThemeTest);
        * windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon = the EXISTING launcher foreground
          (Phase 38.1's ">_" glyph, no new asset). On Android 12+ the platform
          animates it; on API 24-30 androidx.core:core-splashscreen backports
          the same behaviour (the ONLY new dependency of the 50-52 series);
        * postSplashScreenTheme = the app theme the activity has always used.

      The splash is dismissed by code, never by a timer: MainActivity installs
      it and keeps it until the pure LaunchReadiness policy says the theme and
      the first route are known (and a crash overlay or safe-mode start always
      win). See ui/crash/LaunchReadiness.kt.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Codec.Splash" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/codec_splash_background</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.MyApplication</item>
    </style>
</resources>
